      "writtenOn": "2019-01-24T23:46:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there any command which evaluates rv as \u0027the length of output data returned\u0027?\n\nIf not, my first option is to change ec_command for good:\n\n  int ec_command(...)\n  {\n    int rv \u003d ec_command_proto(...);\n    return rv \u003c 0 ? rv : 0;\n  }\n\nEven if there are such commands, we can make them call ec_command_proto or change ec_command to:\n\n  int ec_command(..., int *insize);\n\nOr apply CMD_RETURN(rv) everywhere. Thank you for cleaning up the mess whatever option you choose.\n\n\u003e I think it would reduce future mistakes\n\nI agree. If we don\u0027t fix this comprehensively, I think we will keep making the same mistake.",
